@using System.Globalization
@using BlazorAtoms.Tabs

<PageTitle>Tabs Playground</PageTitle>

<h1>Tabs playground</h1>
<p><code>AtomTabs</code> owns the selected value; <code>AtomTab</code> and <code>AtomTabPanel</code> pair
   up by a string <code>Value</code>. Two named slots (<code>TabList</code> and <code>Panels</code>)
   rather than one flat child list, because Blazor renders children in source order — interleaved tabs
   and panels could not be laid out as a strip above a panel region without hoisting nodes across the
   render tree, which the framework can't do.</p>
<p>Full ARIA tabs pattern: <code>tablist</code>/<code>tab</code>/<code>tabpanel</code> roles,
   <code>aria-selected</code>, <code>aria-controls</code>&harr;<code>aria-labelledby</code> id pairs,
   roving <code>tabindex</code>, and Arrow/Home/End navigation. <strong>Click a tab, then try the
   arrow keys</strong> &mdash; and <code>Ctrl+Home</code>, which scrolls the page instead of jumping to
   the first tab.</p>
<p>One small self-imported JS module (<code>atom-tabs.js</code>) cancels the browser's default scroll for
   exactly the keys the component consumes, per axis &mdash; Blazor decides
   <code>:preventDefault</code> at render time, so it can't be applied per key without also swallowing
   <code>Tab</code>. Nothing to wire up, and the tabs still navigate if it fails to load. Try
   <code>Orientation="Vertical"</code> with a tall page: that's the case where the missing guard was
   visible.</p>
<p><a href="playground/cardlayout">&larr; Card layout playground</a></p>

<div class="tab-controls">
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Variant</label>
        <select @bind="VariantSel">
            @foreach (var v in Variants) { <option value="@v">@v</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Size</label>
        <select @bind="SizeSel">
            @foreach (var s in Sizes) { <option value="@s">@s</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Orientation</label>
        <select @bind="OrientationSel">
            @foreach (var o in Orientations) { <option value="@o">@o</option> }
        </select>
        <span class="note">also sets aria-orientation, which picks the arrow keys</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Align</label>
        <select @bind="AlignSel">
            @foreach (var a in Aligns) { <option value="@a">@a</option> }
        </select>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Effect</label>
        <select @bind="EffectSel">
            @foreach (var e in Effects) { <option value="@e">@e</option> }
        </select>
        <span class="note">CSS only &mdash; no C# state</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ActivationMode</label>
        <select @bind="ActivationSel">
            @foreach (var a in Activations) { <option value="@a">@a</option> }
        </select>
        <span class="note">Manual: arrows move focus, Enter selects</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>PanelRender</label>
        <select @bind="PanelRenderSel">
            @foreach (var r in PanelRenders) { <option value="@r">@r</option> }
        </select>
        <span class="note">type in the Bravo panel's box, switch away and back</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Tabs (comma-separated)</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="TabsCsv" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(no tabs)" />
        <span class="note">@TabKeys.Count tab(s)</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>AriaLabel</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="AriaLabelV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(none)" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Content</label>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="tabIcon" @bind="ShowIcons" /><label for="tabIcon" class="inline">Icon slot</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="tabBadge" @bind="ShowBadge" /><label for="tabBadge" class="inline">Badge on 2nd tab</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="tabCustom" @bind="CustomCaption" /><label for="tabCustom" class="inline">ChildContent on 1st tab</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="tabDis" @bind="DisableThird" /><label for="tabDis" class="inline">Disable 3rd tab</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="tabScroll" @bind="ScrollableV" /><label for="tabScroll" class="inline">Scrollable strip</label></div>
        <div class="row"><input type="checkbox" id="tabVis" @bind="VisibleV" /><label for="tabVis" class="inline">Visible</label></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>IndicatorThickness (px, 0=default) <span class="val">@IndicatorThicknessV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="10" step="1" @bind="IndicatorThicknessV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Radius (px, -1=default) <span class="val">@RadiusV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="-1" max="28" step="1" @bind="RadiusV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>PanelPadding (px, -1=default) <span class="val">@PanelPaddingV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="-1" max="48" step="1" @bind="PanelPaddingV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
        <span class="note">cascades; a panel's own Padding wins</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Panel 1 Padding (px, -1=inherit) <span class="val">@Panel1PaddingV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="-1" max="48" step="1" @bind="Panel1PaddingV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Gap (px, -1=default) <span class="val">@GapV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="-1" max="24" step="1" @bind="GapV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>FontSize (px, 0=Size) <span class="val">@FontSizeV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="28" step="1" @bind="FontSizeV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Duration (s, 0=default) <span class="val">@DurationV.ToString(Inv)</span></label>
        <input type="range" min="0" max="1.5" step="0.05" @bind="DurationV" @bind:event="oninput" @bind:culture="Inv" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>AccentColor</label>
        <div class="row color">
            <input type="color" @bind="AccentPick" @bind:event="oninput" />
            <input type="text" @bind="AccentColorV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(#2563eb)" />
            <button type="button" class="clr-btn" @onclick="@(() => AccentColorV = "")">clear</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>TabColor</label>
        <div class="row color">
            <input type="color" @bind="TabPick" @bind:event="oninput" />
            <input type="text" @bind="TabColorV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(muted ink)" />
            <button type="button" class="clr-btn" @onclick="@(() => TabColorV = "")">clear</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>ActiveTabColor</label>
        <div class="row color">
            <input type="color" @bind="ActiveTabPick" @bind:event="oninput" />
            <input type="text" @bind="ActiveTabColorV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(accent)" />
            <button type="button" class="clr-btn" @onclick="@(() => ActiveTabColorV = "")">clear</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>IndicatorColor</label>
        <div class="row color">
            <input type="color" @bind="IndicatorPick" @bind:event="oninput" />
            <input type="text" @bind="IndicatorColorV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(accent)" />
            <button type="button" class="clr-btn" @onclick="@(() => IndicatorColorV = "")">clear</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>BorderColor</label>
        <div class="row color">
            <input type="color" @bind="BorderPick" @bind:event="oninput" />
            <input type="text" @bind="BorderColorV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(currentColor tint)" />
            <button type="button" class="clr-btn" @onclick="@(() => BorderColorV = "")">clear</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>PanelBackgroundColor</label>
        <div class="row color">
            <input type="color" @bind="PanelBgPick" @bind:event="oninput" />
            <input type="text" @bind="PanelBgV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(transparent)" />
            <button type="button" class="clr-btn" @onclick="@(() => PanelBgV = "")">clear</button>
        </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>CssClass</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="CssClassV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="(none)" />
    </div>
    <div class="ctrl">
        <label>Style</label>
        <input type="text" @bind="StyleV" @bind:event="oninput" placeholder="e.g. max-width:40rem" />
    </div>
</div>

<div class="tab-stage">
    <section class="tab-case">
        <h2>AtomTabs</h2>
        <AtomTabs @bind-Value="ActiveTab"
                  Variant="@VariantSel" Size="@SizeSel" Orientation="@OrientationSel"
                  Align="@AlignSel" Effect="@EffectSel"
                  ActivationMode="@ActivationSel" PanelRender="@PanelRenderSel"
                  Scrollable="@ScrollableV" Visible="@VisibleV"
                  AriaLabel="@Nz(AriaLabelV)"
                  AccentColor="@Nz(AccentColorV)" TabColor="@Nz(TabColorV)"
                  ActiveTabColor="@Nz(ActiveTabColorV)" IndicatorColor="@Nz(IndicatorColorV)"
                  IndicatorThickness="@Opt(IndicatorThicknessV)"
                  BorderColor="@Nz(BorderColorV)" PanelBackgroundColor="@Nz(PanelBgV)"
                  Radius="@Signed(RadiusV)" PanelPadding="@Signed(PanelPaddingV)"
                  Gap="@Signed(GapV)" FontSize="@Opt(FontSizeV)" Duration="@Opt(DurationV)"
                  CssClass="@Nz(CssClassV)" Style="@Nz(StyleV)">
            <TabList>
                @foreach (var (key, index) in TabKeys.Select((k, i) => (k, i)))
                {
                    <AtomTab Value="@key"
                             Title="@key"
                             Icon="@(ShowIcons ? IconFor(index) : null)"
                             Badge="@(ShowBadge && index == 1 ? "3" : null)"
                             Disabled="@(DisableThird && index == 2)"
                             ChildContent="@(CustomCaption && index == 0 ? CustomFirstCaption : null)" />
                }
            </TabList>
            <Panels>
                @foreach (var (key, index) in TabKeys.Select((k, i) => (k, i)))
                {
                    <AtomTabPanel Value="@key" Padding="@(index == 0 ? Signed(Panel1PaddingV) : null)">
                        <h3>@key</h3>
                        @if (index == 1)
                        {
                            <p>Type below, switch tabs and come back &mdash; the text survives on
                               <code>Always</code> and <code>Lazy</code>, and is lost on
                               <code>Active</code>, which removes the panel from the DOM.</p>
                            <input type="text" class="tab-probe" placeholder="uncommitted input" />
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
                                of the strip lands here.
                            </p>
                            <p>
                                Panel content for <code>@key</code>. The panel is focusable, so Tab out
